  "split_decision": "Separate the complete concrete stored-class existence wrapper from the arbitrary class-of-perfect-complex proof wrapper. Keep bridge compatibility interfaces and their genuine proof projections in exact archives; do not invent absent operator/index equations or alter any source type.",
  "review_notes": [
    "The full original dependent bridge record stores wittImage : KTheoryIndexWittImage R I, an inert source label, and an arbitrary compatibleWithCrystallineIndexBoundary proposition/proof. All M/W/R/I parameters are supplied. The theorem genuinely projects the last proof; it does not construct the bridge.",
    "The exact inspected WittRealization source has a typed realize function and an independent arbitrary Chern-compatibility proposition. Its image record has a genuine equality image = R.realize I.indexClass. That actual supplied equality is acknowledged, without inferring a Chern character or operator-index compatibility law.",
    "The inspected WittComplex target has dependent degree/element data and chosen zero, optional Type-valued differential/Frobenius/Verschiebung data, and an unrelated isComplex proposition/proof. No de Rham-Witt operations/laws or actual complex differential is constructed.",
    "Although WittValuedIndex is imported, this bridge does not store its operator parameter or a WittValuedCrystallineIndex value, nor an equation identifying one with wittImage. Preserve the exact context without manufacturing that missing relationship.",
    "Retain both commands byte-exact in GRWTSK archives. No independent crystalline-index computation, true compatibility predicate or bridge inhabitant exists in this file to materialize as maintained mathematics."
  ],
